# UI conventions — Camilo Meza AF

When editing matching UI files, follow the project skills under `.cursor/skills/`:

- `camilo-design-system` — palette, Raleway, dark mode, CTA gradient
- `ui-components-patterns` — Layout, SectionsLayout, AnimatedText, Button, cards, nav
- `framer-motion-standards` — useInView + stagger timings
- `financial-landing-ux` — section jobs, hero budget, accessibility, conversion
- `forms-and-feedback` — Formik/Yup + successAlert/errorAlert

## Must follow

1. Do not invent a new color palette; use Tailwind tokens from `tailwind.config.js`.
2. Reuse existing layout/CTA/link components before creating new primitives.
3. Mobile-first (`md:`, `lg:`) and always pair `dark:` styles for new surfaces.
4. Keep Spanish copy for user-facing UI and a professional financial-advisory tone.
5. Prefer one primary conversion CTA hierarchy; avoid clutter in the first viewport.
